{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PDmVxmLC4xUQJMU6k7Qt8d","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tname: supervised-loop-macos-operating-lessons\n3\tdescription: \"2026-09-01 supervised-unpause lessons — integrate from trunk root only, the rollup-compile + drawn-round duties until WI-558/WI-559 land, and this Mac's box traps\"\n4\tmetadata: \n5\t  node_type: memory\n6\t  type: project\n7\t  originSessionId: 57c88b47-5469-4e50-bc76-c5299aeea493\n8\t  modified: 2026-09-01T12:18:43.669Z\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\tFrom the 2026-09-01 supervised unpause (5 rows merged: WI-543/552/553/563/566; decisions 47–51):\n12\t\n13\t- **Until WI-558 lands**, every merge needs the supervisor to compile `docs/reviews/WI-<n>-REVIEW-A.md` on the lane from the round files (time-ordered, governing line last) — the verdict gate requires it and nothing writes it. **Until WI-559 lands**, adjudication lanes get NO review round yet their exit banner claims \"review round approved\" — draw a real round via an independent Opus subagent with a hostile brief (the drawn rounds caught real defects twice: a live --strict ERROR and a 17-row census inflation).\n14\t- **Run `integrate.py` from the TRUNK root, never from inside a lane worktree** — the auto-unload deletes the script's own directory mid-run and post-merge intake crashes (`ModuleNotFoundError: intake`), leaving disposition drafts unminted. Recovery: call `intake.intake_after_merge` directly with the merge's own scope; `intake.py sweep` is structurally unusable (it sweeps ALL terminal folders and the OI-70 guard bites pre-convention rows like WI-457 — kit defect, decision 49).\n15\t- **Refresh-conflict remedy** (generated files only, precedent 52faa5d8): merge trunk into the lane, REGENERATE the conflicted artifacts (gen_trajectory, derive_stage), commit, then re-note the rollup so it stays the newest commit — the verdict clock peels only the station's self-attested refresh commits.\n16\t- **The refresh trunk step regenerates the `[generated]` artifacts but NOT the approval brief `docs/ratify/CURRENT.md`** — so a lane that resolved a CURRENT.md merge conflict by taking trunk's side REDS the refresh bar's `approval-fresh` check until you run `trace.py --approve modified --out docs/ratify/CURRENT.md` on the branch and commit. Hit executing OI-71 (WI-555, 2026-09-01). The refresh is fail-closed: a red bar `reset --hard`s the branch and leaves trunk untouched, so measuring the merge is safe. A transient `git: Unable to write index` can abort the `--no-ff` step with trunk untouched — just retry once merge-ready.\n17\t- **OI-71 done (WI-555, 2026-09-01)**: the held wi508 lane was converted complete→partial MANUALLY (create local ref at the origin HELD branch = \"rename back\"; `git mv` the spec archive/complete→active to undo the self-close; `handback.close_partial`; then `integrate.py integrate` from trunk root) and merged (trunk→551d1b2c). It minted disposition **WI-568**, which owns the keep/discard split and the last_approved REGENERATION (never copy the branch bytes). Flagged to WI-568: LLR-203/204 land Approved (branch's pre-OI-72 commit 580df781) vs OI-72's \"four Drafted rows\" reading.\n18\t- **This Mac's traps**: bare `python` doesn't exist (use .venv or python3 — workers hit 127 three times); the lane pre-commit hook resolves ruff via SYSTEM python3 → loud format-SKIP on every worktree commit; never chain the loop launch into a compound foreground Bash (2-min timeout killed it mid-claim once — parked branch resumed fine).\n19\t- The claim-refusal on status.md prose ids applies to ANY hand-authored mention including an embedded supervisor prompt (decision 47). OpenAI provider limit resets ~08:40 UTC; rounds before that run `-relaxed` (record them).\n20\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f1f30fa6-1e6b-4860-95af-a97b48cbf977","uuid":"90bee220-8544-45a2-b915-455114054163","timestamp":"2026-09-03T03:11:29.595Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/diytechy/.claude/projects/-Users-diytechy-Documents-ai-template/memory/supervised-loop-macos-operating-lessons.md","content":"---\nname: supervised-loop-macos-operating-lessons\ndescription: \"2026-09-01 supervised-unpause lessons — integrate from trunk root only, the rollup-compile + drawn-round duties until WI-558/WI-559 land, and this Mac's box traps\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 57c88b47-5469-4e50-bc76-c5299aeea493\n  modified: 2026-09-01T12:18:43.669Z\n---\n\nFrom the 2026-09-01 supervised unpause (5 rows merged: WI-543/552/553/563/566; decisions 47–51):\n\n- **Until WI-558 lands**, every merge needs the supervisor to compile `docs/reviews/WI-<n>-REVIEW-A.md` on the lane from the round files (time-ordered, governing line last) — the verdict gate requires it and nothing writes it. **Until WI-559 lands**, adjudication lanes get NO review round yet their exit banner claims \"review round approved\" — draw a real round via an independent Opus subagent with a hostile brief (the drawn rounds caught real defects twice: a live --strict ERROR and a 17-row census inflation).\n- **Run `integrate.py` from the TRUNK root, never from inside a lane worktree** — the auto-unload deletes the script's own directory mid-run and post-merge intake crashes (`ModuleNotFoundError: intake`), leaving disposition drafts unminted. Recovery: call `intake.intake_after_merge` directly with the merge's own scope; `intake.py sweep` is structurally unusable (it sweeps ALL terminal folders and the OI-70 guard bites pre-convention rows like WI-457 — kit defect, decision 49).\n- **Refresh-conflict remedy** (generated files only, precedent 52faa5d8): merge trunk into the lane, REGENERATE the conflicted artifacts (gen_trajectory, derive_stage), commit, then re-note the rollup so it stays the newest commit — the verdict clock peels only the station's self-attested refresh commits.\n- **The refresh trunk step regenerates the `[generated]` artifacts but NOT the approval brief `docs/ratify/CURRENT.md`** — so a lane that resolved a CURRENT.md merge conflict by taking trunk's side REDS the refresh bar's `approval-fresh` check until you run `trace.py --approve modified --out docs/ratify/CURRENT.md` on the branch and commit. Hit executing OI-71 (WI-555, 2026-09-01). The refresh is fail-closed: a red bar `reset --hard`s the branch and leaves trunk untouched, so measuring the merge is safe. A transient `git: Unable to write index` can abort the `--no-ff` step with trunk untouched — just retry once merge-ready.\n- **OI-71 done (WI-555, 2026-09-01)**: the held wi508 lane was converted complete→partial MANUALLY (create local ref at the origin HELD branch = \"rename back\"; `git mv` the spec archive/complete→active to undo the self-close; `handback.close_partial`; then `integrate.py integrate` from trunk root) and merged (trunk→551d1b2c). It minted disposition **WI-568**, which owns the keep/discard split and the last_approved REGENERATION (never copy the branch bytes). Flagged to WI-568: LLR-203/204 land Approved (branch's pre-OI-72 commit 580df781) vs OI-72's \"four Drafted rows\" reading.\n- **This Mac's traps**: bare `python` doesn't exist (use .venv or python3 — workers hit 127 three times); the lane pre-commit hook resolves ruff via SYSTEM python3 → loud format-SKIP on every worktree commit; never chain the loop launch into a compound foreground Bash (2-min timeout killed it mid-claim once — parked branch resumed fine).\n- The claim-refusal on status.md prose ids applies to ANY hand-authored mention including an embedded supervisor prompt (decision 47). OpenAI provider limit resets ~08:40 UTC; rounds before that run `-relaxed` (record them).\n","numLines":20,"startLine":1,"totalLines":20}}}
