{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CefmrHJ51xz5WFg6RbVvM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"WI-579 is done and the tree is clean.\n\n## What I found\n\nThe three review-A findings had already been fixed by the prior session. I verified each independently rather than trusting the claim:\n\n- **MAJOR 1** — `review_owed_by_evidence` now routes through `kverdict.branch_entries` (i.e. `branch_paths`/`logged_rounds`/`round_entries`) with the worker's base and branch. The BUILD-session regression is real: `tests/test_verdict_record.py:516` adds a round with `session_phase=\"BUILD\"` and asserts *both* readers still refuse it.\n- **MAJOR 2** — `_round_refusal` compares the stamped trailer against `round_count(entries)` and refuses a mismatch; `rounds=<N>` is now defined as completed cycles at the governing tree (max per-phase count). Regression at line 311 drives the exact `rounds=0` vs `rounds=1` case.\n- **MINOR 3** — LLR-207's rationale is a standing technical reason with the OI-76 provenance removed.\n\n## What I added\n\nVerifying finding 1 surfaced residue the fix left behind: `review_owed_by_evidence` still took a **`reviews_dir` parameter that nothing read**. The fix replaced the directory scan with the committed-path walk but kept the argument — a parameter naming a directory the function no longer opens, on the one reader whose defect *was* reading that directory. Dropped it and the `resume_owed_round` pass-through (`0b1f3b41`). The caller keeps its own `reviews_dir` local, which the verdict-path and scoreboard slots still use — I checked before deleting, and a test local I nearly removed turned out to still be used at line 529.\n\nI also drove the row's own machinery over the row's own history, the only end-to-end check available for a rule about trees:\n\n| commit | touched | identity |\n|---|---|---|\n| `41b84e93` spec + fragment | `docs/archive/work/` + `docs/log.d/` | `6f314694…` |\n| `7098ad21` telemetry | `docs/iteration/` + `docs/reviews/` only | `6f314694…` |\n\nThe unchanged identity across a telemetry commit **is** the double-round defect class this WI kills.\n\n## Bars\n\n- Smoke: **1500 passed, 8 skipped, 24.25s**; budget **26.8s vs 60s → within**; `check_docs` **0 broken**.\n- Full unfiltered suite at the tip: **3339 passed, 24 skipped, 1 failed in 624.14s**. The one failure is `test_this_repo_s_committed_stage_is_current` — the trunk-owned `docs/stage` assertion already diagnosed and bisected to pass at the integration base. No new failure; I ran this specifically because removing a parameter is what a grep can miss and `test_agent_loop.py` sits outside the smoke tier.\n\nClose was already correct (Deliverable before Context, `specref` cleared, claim drained, ratify brief verified current). All five spine rows are `Drafted`, no status flipped, `last_approved/` untouched — no approval act performed.\n\n**The lane now owes a fresh round** (`round_count: 0` at tree `454f8fae…`; the existing round names `0c7cb4e`). That draw is the reviewer's act — I did not author one. I have not pushed.\n\nOne thing worth flagging separately: a mis-scoped `grep` from a persisted `cd` returned empty and read as a clean check during this session. I caught it, re-ran correctly, and recorded it in memory — verifying a *negative* is where that failure mode hides, since no output is the expected answer."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":240,"cache_read_input_tokens":123343,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":240},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f1f30fa6-1e6b-4860-95af-a97b48cbf977","uuid":"32b53b51-0d16-4c24-8894-40e0aac057b5","request_id":"req_011CefmrGUhi9JpcdP62P3aj"}
